e Lake Tahoe Basin. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. Which of the following statements best describes the association between the elevation and the temperature of locations in the Lake Tahoe Basin?</p></p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">As the elevation increases, the temperature tends to increase.</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">As the elevation increases, the temperature tends to decrease.</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">As the elevation decreases, the temperature tends to decrease.</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">There is no association between the elevation and the temperature.</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The association between the elevation and the temperature of locations in the Lake Tahoe Basin can be described by looking at the direction of the line of best fit. The line of best fit slopes downward, which&nbsp;corresponds to the temperature decreasing as the elevation increases.<p>Choices A and C are incorrect. Both of these choices would be represented by a line of best fit that slopes from the lower left to the upper right of the graph, which isn&rsquo;t what&rsquo;s shown on the graph. Choice D is incorrect. This choice would be represented by a line of best fit that is horizontal or has a slope very close to 0. This is not what&rsquo;s shown on the graph.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":1,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959633,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"661dfddd","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1691007959633,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"070913-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"d2c0d94f-3887-4b96-b2d3-1b97635a9169","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"070913-DC","s