	<mn>3</mn>
	<mn>20</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>, feet per second.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"674a4084","external_id":"e098ab1f-ca25-4df4-862e-fe8448392a67","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"d97d6045-368d-4400-bc4f-8025d474dac3","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">An insect moves at a speed of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"three twentieths\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac></math> feet per second. What is this speed, in <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">yards</span> per second?&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 3 feet  equals 1 yard right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yard</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5b694c46-65ea-4f05-9ef4-a87d60845f91","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one twentieth\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>20</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e85934e1-800a-46b4-8b0f-dbb2e1e1033b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"nine twentieths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t<mn>20</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"09d9d2eb-193b-4122-98be-e68de674aa6e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"573fa320-daf4-4163-805c-975b25d68aa6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["5b694c46-65ea-4f05-9ef4-a87d60845f91"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"3 feet  equals 1 yard\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yard</mtext></math>. It follows that a speed of <math alttext=\"three twentieths\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t<mn>20</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</m