ath/MathML\" alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"60,000 equals p\"><mn>60,000</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"60,000\"><mn>60,000</mn></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"699af7b3","skill_cd":"Q.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Percentages","createDate":1776362727992,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"36bef1c8-d853-462f-a9e8-7575812e84e9","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"726d5b93-0414-4cc1-b1f1-8fafc4013950","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"spr","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The weight of sample A is <math alttext=\"468 percent sign\"><mn>468</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the weight of sample B, and the weight of sample A is <math alttext=\"0.780 percent sign\"><mn>0.780</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the weight of sample C. If the weight of sample C is <math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of the weight of sample B, what is the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["60000"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"60,000\"><mn>60,000</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the weight of sample A is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"468 percent sign\"><mn>468</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the weight of sample B&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0.780 percent sign\"><mn>0.780</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the weight of sample C. Let the weight of sample B be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=