\"></line><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"111.11180114746094\" y=\"132\" height=\"140\" width=\"31.736024856567383\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(126.97981357574463 291.84)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">A</text><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"174.5838508605957\" y=\"192\" height=\"80\" width=\"31.736024856567383\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(190.4518632888794 291.84)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">B</text><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"238.05590057373047\" y=\"92\" height=\"180\" width=\"31.736024856567383\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(253.92391300201416 291.84)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">C</text><rect xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"301.52795028686523\" y=\"242\" height=\"30\" width=\"31.736024856567383\" fill=\"#B3B3B3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"mitre\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"></rect><text xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(317.3959627151489 291.84)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">D</text><text text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(222.18788814544678 24)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\"> </text><text text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(222.18788814544678 48)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\"> </text><text text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"translate(222.18788814544678 325.67999999999995)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">Gift</text></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for bar graph\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>The Number of volunteers data for the 4 bars are as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>A: 14</li>\n<li>B: 8</li>\n<li>C: 18</li>\n<li>D: 3</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In April, there were <math alttext=\"43\"><mn>43</mn>\n</math> volunteers in a cleanup project. Each volunteer was asked to choose a small gift labeled A, B, C, or D. The bar graph shows the number of volunteers who chose each gift. How many volunteers chose gift C?</p>","type":"mcq","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1730147357403,"updateDate":1730147357403}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357403, 1730147357403),
    ($SATQ$6e4a60dd$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$14922-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Rita&rsquo;s total bill at a restaurant was $25.00, including tax. If she left a tip of 20% of the total bill, what was the amount of the tip?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>$3.50</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>$4.00</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>$4.50</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>$5.00</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The total bill was $25.00. The percentage 20% is equivalent to the decimal 0.2. The tip is the product of the percentage and the total bill; therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6e4a60dd/img_000_26bc9c22.png" alt="0 point 2 times 25, equals 5"></span>, so the tip was $5.00.<p>Choices A, B, and C are incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly converting the given percentage or a calculation error.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"6e4a60dd","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"14922-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Rita&rsquo;s total bill at a restaurant was $25.00, including tax. If she left a tip of 20% of the total bill, what was the amount of the tip?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p>$3.50</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>$4.00</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>$4.50</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>$5.00</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The total bill was $25.00. The percentage 20% is equivalent to the decimal 0.2. The tip is the product of the percentage and the total bill; therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6e4a60dd/img_000_26bc9c22.png\" alt=\"0 point 2 times 25, equals 5\"></span>, so the tip was $5.00.<p>Choices A, B, and C are incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly converting the given percentage or a calculation error.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":1,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959639,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"6e4a60dd","skill_cd":"Q.B.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Percentages","createDate":1691007959639,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"14922-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"e2bbc646-7a91-4c1e-b01d-379a58a7015d","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"14922-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Rita&rsquo;s total bill at a restaurant was $25.00, including tax. If she left a tip of 20% of the total bill, what was the amount of the tip?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>$3.50</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>$4.00</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>$4.50</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>$5.00</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The total bill was $25.00. The percentage 20% is equivalent to the decimal 0.2. The tip is the product of the percentage and the total bill; therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 point 2 times 25, equals 5\"></span>, so the tip was $5.00.<p>Choices A, B, and C are incorrect and may be the result of incorrectly converting the given percentage or a calculation error.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959639,"updateDate":1691007959639}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959639, 1691007959639),
    ($SATQ$6fca0144$SATQ$, $SATQ$4c42a273-cc25-495c-8315-77ecc0dd2ea9$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.G.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Evaluating statistical claims: Observational studies and experiments $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">For a baobab tree habitat in South Africa, a scientist randomly selected <math alttext="50"><mn>50</mn>
</math> baobab trees that were <math alttext="17"><mn>17</mn>
</math> years old and randomly assigned them to two groups. Each group was subjected to a different watering pattern for <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> consecutive years to observe whether the watering pattern affects the trees&rsquo; growth rate. Based on the design of the study, what is the largest group to which these results can be applied?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"fb10b45b-f0c9-401d-a3bc-8bcc9dfe53d1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> baobab trees that were selected in this habitat&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"b68c06d4-7313-43c1-9ab5-85912ddbf724","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the baobab trees that were <math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math> years old in this habitat</p>"},{"id":"287f324b-142a-4d7e-84db-1cb9e644b787","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the baobab trees that were <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math> years old in South Africa</p>"},{"id":"82bf1f5d-d294-44c6-8a85-52d98e01951e","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the baobab trees that were <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math> years old in this habitat</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["82bf1f5d-d294-44c6-8a85-52d98e01951e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. When a study uses a randomly selected sample, the largest group to which the results of the study can be applied is the population from which the sample was selected. It's given that the scientist randomly selected the trees from the baobab trees in a certain habitat that were <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="17"><mn>17</mn></math> years old. Therefore, the largest group to which the results of this study can be applied is all the baobab trees that were <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="17"><mn>17</mn></math> years old in this habitat.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. Since the sample was randomly selected from a population, the results can be applied to a larger group than the sample.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect. The sample was selected from a population of baobab trees that were <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="17"><mn>17</mn></math> years old, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="19"><mn>19</mn></math> years old.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. The sample was selected from a certain tree habitat in South Africa, not from all the baobab trees that were <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="17"><mn>17</mn></math> years old&nbsp;in South Africa.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6fca0144","external_id":"4c42a273-cc25-495c-8315-77ecc0dd2ea9","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"ed1883e1-6c73-4c01-9d60-0f3ec131f76d","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.G.","skill_desc":"Evaluating statistical claims: Observational studies and experiments ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For a baobab tree habitat in South Africa, a scientist randomly selected <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> baobab trees that were <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math> years old and randomly assigned them to two groups. Each group was subjected to a different watering pattern for <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> consecutive years to observe whether the watering pattern affects the trees&rsquo; growth rate. Based on the design of the study, what is the largest group to which these results can be applied?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"fb10b45b-f0c9-401d-a3bc-8bcc9dfe53d1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> baobab trees that were selected in this habitat&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"b68c06d4-7313-43c1-9ab5-85912ddbf724","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the baobab trees that were <math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math> years old in this habitat</p>"},{"id":"287f324b-142a-4d7e-84db-1cb9e644b787","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the baobab trees that were <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math> years old in South Africa</p>"},{"id":"82bf1f5d-d294-44c6-8a85-52d98e01951e","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">All the baobab trees that were <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math> years old in this habitat</p>"}],"keys":["82bf1f5d-d294-44c6-8a85-52d98e01951e"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. When a study uses a randomly selected sample, the largest group to which the results of the study can be applied is the population from which the sample was selected. It's given that the scientist randomly selected the trees from the baobab trees in a certain habitat that were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> years old. Therefore, the largest group to which the results of this study can be applied is all the baobab trees that were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> years old in this habitat.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. Since the sample was randomly selected from a population, the results can be applied to a larger group than the sample.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. The sample was selected from a population of baobab trees that were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> years old, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn></math> years old.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. The sample was selected from a certain tree habitat in South Africa, not from all the baobab trees that were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> years old&nbsp;in South Africa.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017718,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"6fca0144","skill_cd":"Q.G.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Evaluating statistical claims: Observational studies and experiments ","createDate":1755117017718,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Pro