value in ordered data set B is less than the respective value in ordered data set A. Therefore, conceptually, the mean of data set A must be greater than the mean of data set B.</p><p>Choices A, B, and C are incorrect and may result from various misconceptions or miscalculations.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959622,"updateDate":1691007959622}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959622, 1691007959622),
    ($SATQ$709e04de$SATQ$, $SATQ$f518f607-0819-47bd-b33b-db922ee03cb2$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$404d0e86-6fe2-4b4c-a04d-cd6b20f3391a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="1.13"><mn>1.13</mn>
</math> times <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>. The value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> is what percent greater than <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f492c516-5606-4089-a743-8ca7165a254c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"11.3\"><mn>11.3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"616d2dc0-7584-48d4-a30a-28f6d489cbd0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fa2127e4-8c0c-460f-8d75-925e52a5db75","content":"<p><math alttext=\"130\"><mn>130</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"01c8004c-e721-455e-a3a4-740b12b5bd70","content":"<p><math alttext=\"213\"><mn>213</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["616d2dc0-7584-48d4-a30a-28f6d489cbd0"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="1.13"><mn>1.13</mn></math> times <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>. This can be written as <math alttext="z equals left parenthesis 1.13 right parenthesis left parenthesis 100 right parenthesis"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>1.13</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="z equals left parenthesis 1 plus 0.13 right parenthesis left parenthesis 100 right parenthesis"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.13</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math alttext="z equals left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction 13 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis 100 right parenthesis"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced></math>. It follows that the value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="100 percent sign"><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math> plus <math alttext="13 percent sign"><mn>13</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="13 percent sign"><mn>13</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This gives a value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> that is <math alttext="1.113"><mn>1.113</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="1.13"><mn>1.13</mn>
</math>, times <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This gives a value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> that is <math alttext="2.30"><mn>2.30</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="1.13"><mn>1.13</mn>
</math>, times <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This gives a value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> that is <math alttext="3.13"><mn>3.13</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="1.13"><mn>1.13</mn>
</math>, times <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"709e04de","external_id":"f518f607-0819-47bd-b33b-db922ee03cb2","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"404d0e86-6fe2-4b4c-a04d-cd6b20f3391a","uId":"7f75152b-97c9-4919-8ed2-bd4670746c7c","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The value of <math alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"1.13\"><mn>1.13</mn>\n</math> times <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math>. The value of <math alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi>\n</math> is what percent greater than <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f492c516-5606-4089-a743-8ca7165a254c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"11.3\"><mn>11.3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"616d2dc0-7584-48d4-a30a-28f6d489cbd0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fa2127e4-8c0c-460f-8d75-925e52a5db75","content":"<p><math alttext=\"130\"><mn>130</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"01c8004c-e721-455e-a3a4-740b12b5bd70","content":"<p><math alttext=\"213\"><mn>213</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["616d2dc0-7584-48d4-a30a-28f6d489cbd0"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the value of <math alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"1.13\"><mn>1.13</mn></math> times <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math>. This can be written as <math alttext=\"z equals left parenthesis 1.13 right parenthesis left parenthesis 100 right parenthesis\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>1.13</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"z equals left parenthesis 1 plus 0.13 right parenthesis left parenthesis 1