$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The line graph shows the number of graduates from the classes of 2001 through 2007 at a certain school who enrolled in college within 24 months of graduation. Of the following, which class had the fewest graduates who enrolled in college within 24 months of graduation?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">2002</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">2004</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">2005</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph block_choice\">2007</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. The year with the fewest graduates who enrolled in college within 24 months of graduation is the point with the lowest value on the vertical axis. This occurs at 2002.<p>Choice B, C, and D are incorrect. The years 2004, 2005, and 2007 each had a greater number of graduates who enrolled in college within 24 months of graduation than did the year 2002.</p></p>
